  "about": "The classic 1993 first-person shooter, running from PSRAM on the ESP32-P4 via PrBoom. The store fetches the free shareware episode (doom1.wad) and prboom.wad onto the card on first launch; drop in your own doom.wad or doom2.wad for the full game. Screen setting: 640x400 (the 320x200 picture doubled, the default: sharp and the least to send each frame), 800x480 (the classic 768x480) or 960x600 (tripled, the panel's full height).",
  "changelog": "0.2.4: cache WAD data in PSRAM to reduce SD-card stalls while loading levels.\n0.2.3: output audio at 48 kHz, report sound renderer timing and stop audio cleanly when returning to the launcher.\n0.2.2: respond to the launcher close signal before rendering the next frame.\n0.2.0: canvas from the store's Screen setting: 640x400 (2x, default), 800x480 (2.4x) or 960x600 (3x)",
